To: tradesprior@gmail.com

Post-AGI Alpha Hunt =E2=80=94 10 Sep 2026

Highest-signal fresh rabbit holes

   1. INTERFACE-CHEMISTRY DENSITY =E2=80=94 hidden consumables scale faster=
 than
   package count

The best new small-cap exposure this run is MEC Company (TSE:4971). MEC=E2=
=80=99s
CZ-series chemistry prepares copper surfaces so resin layers adhere
reliably inside semiconductor package substrates. The key point is not
merely that AI packaging demand is rising: MEC states that as package
substrates become larger and adopt more layers, the amount of CZ chemistry
used increases. That gives us a new primitive: interface_density =E2=80=94 =
the
number/area of critical material interfaces that must be chemically
conditioned per package.

This is a cleaner second derivative on chiplet/HBM/CoWoS complexity than
substrate unit volumes alone. MEC says CZ is ~60% of chemical sales and is
widely adopted by package-substrate makers; Q1 CZ sales rose 41.4% YoY to a
quarterly record, while H1 company operating profit rose 69.4% YoY. Current
market cap is ~=C2=A5114B and forward P/E ~16.7x after a major rerating, so=
 it
is no longer undiscovered, but valuation is still radically different from
many headline AI-equipment names.

Why it matters: AI raises package area, layer count, thermal cycling,
wiring density and reliability requirements simultaneously. Tiny interface
treatments can therefore gain content per device even if semiconductor unit
growth is modest.

Falsifiers: glass-core/direct-bonding architectures eliminate relevant
copper-resin interfaces faster than MEC adapts; advanced packaging demand
shifts toward processes where CZ content/package falls; customer
concentration or chemistry substitution compresses pricing.

Sources:
https://www.mec-co.com/en/ir/investors/business/
https://www.mec-co.com/en/ir/library/pdf/setsumeikai/5801_e.pdf
https://www.mec-co.com/en/ir/library/pdf/report/5801.pdf

   1. VACUUM-CONTENT INFLATION =E2=80=94 process-step complexity may matter=
 more
   than wafers

VAT Group=E2=80=99s H1 2026 semiconductor-valve orders rose 99% YoY while
semiconductor sales fell 13%, pushing valve backlog up 127% YoY. The
striking part is the divergence between orders and delivered sales:
fabs/toolmakers are reserving vacuum hardware well ahead of revenue
realization. VAT added >700 employees in H1 and is trying to push quarterly
output above CHF450M.

New thesis variable: vacuum_content_per_wafer. More ALD/ALE, selective
etch, deposition, cleaning and advanced memory layers can increase the
number/value of vacuum-controlled process steps per wafer even without
equivalent wafer-volume growth.

This is another complexity-density effect analogous to timing-content and
measurement-density inflation.

Caveat: VAT is already expensive; recent valuation screens put forward P/E
around 37x and TTM metrics much higher. Better alpha may lie one layer
below VAT in elastomers, seals, precision-machined valve parts, coatings
and service consumables.

Falsifiers: tool architectures consolidate chambers/process steps; valve
reuse/service intervals lengthen; the current order surge proves mostly
inventory prebuild rather than sustained process-content growth.

Sources:
https://www.vatgroup.com/investor-relations/annual-report/group-results
https://ayondo.com/en/news/CH0311864901/vat-group-ag/vat-media-release-on-h=
alf-year-2026-results-2369620

   1. DOPANT SCARCITY =E2=80=94 the fiber bottleneck has an upstream chemis=
try layer

The optical-fiber boom is becoming obvious, but the less-discussed upstream
constraint is germanium tetrachloride, the ultra-high-purity dopant used to
raise the refractive index of silica fiber cores. China remains dominant in
germanium production and export controls create geopolitical optionality.
The investment implication is that AI optics can pull on a tiny
critical-mineral stream whose supply is largely a by-product of other
mining/refining activity.

New kernel primitive: byproduct_dopant_elasticity =3D incremental qualified
dopant supply / incremental end-market demand. When this is low, a small
optical-fiber demand shock can produce nonlinear pricing.

Potential exposures: Teck and Umicore are real non-Chinese germanium
sources, but both are diversified; the higher-alpha task is to identify
smaller refiners/recyclers capable of producing optical-grade GeCl4 rather
than merely owning germanium-bearing feedstock.

Falsifiers: fiber designs materially reduce Ge loading, alternative dopants
gain qualification, recycling expands rapidly, or Chinese export controls
normalize enough to remove scarcity rents.

Sources:
https://www.reuters.com/business/media-telecom/verizon-signs-optical-fiber-=
deal-with-corning-expand-broadband-support-ai-growth-2026-09-08/
https://introl.com/uk/blog/germanium-chokepoint-china-fiber-optic-supply-ch=
ain-2026

   1. EMBEDDED-UTILITY TOLL ROADS =E2=80=94 gases are capacity rights, not
   commodities

Air Liquide=E2=80=99s April 2026 decision to invest =E2=82=AC200M in two Ja=
panese
ultra-high-purity gas units under a long-term semiconductor customer
agreement illustrates a useful distinction: advanced fabs do not simply buy
commodity nitrogen/argon/oxygen. They rely on qualified, site-specific,
continuously available gas infrastructure that is often financed and
operated under long-term contracts.

Air Products likewise disclosed new Samsung wins involving owned/operated
production facilities and bulk specialty-gas systems.

The hidden asset is therefore not gas itself but embedded qualified utility
capacity sitting physically beside a fab.

New variable: utility_lock_in =3D qualification_cost =C3=97 switching_downt=
ime =C3=97
onsite_asset_specificity =C3=97 contract_duration.

This has lower equity convexity in Air Liquide/Air Products because they
are enormous diversified businesses. Better rabbit hole: Japanese
specialty-gas producers such as Kanto Denka Kogyo, Nippon Sanso, Resonac
and smaller purifier/abatement suppliers.

Falsifiers: fabs aggressively insource gases; commoditization/supplier
competition removes pricing power; semiconductor capacity additions
underperform announced plans.

Sources:
https://www.reuters.com/business/energy/air-liquide-invest-236-million-japa=
n-support-next-generation-ai-chip-production-2026-04-16/
https://www.nasdaq.com/press-release/air-products-reports-fiscal-2026-secon=
d-quarter-results-2026-04-30

   1. PURE-MATERIAL READINESS =E2=80=94 Toyo Gosei shows a different kind o=
f
   qualification debt

Toyo Gosei (TSE:4970) has expanded cutting-edge photosensitive-material
capacity to 1.8x and semiconductor high-purity-solvent shipping capacity to
~3x. Management explicitly says semiconductor innovation is now moving so
quickly that when customers ask for a new material there is no longer time
to develop the underlying technology from scratch; capacity and R&D must
exist in advance.

That is direct evidence for our qualification-debt thesis: suppliers must
spend before demand is contractually certain because customer innovation
cycles are shorter than chemical qualification/build cycles.

The stock is small (~=C2=A584B market cap) but has roughly doubled in value=
 over
the past year and remains operationally volatile; recent TTM earnings were
negative despite long-term AI-linked materials demand.

New signal: prequalification_capex_ratio =3D capacity/R&D committed before
customer production qualification divided by current revenue. High values
can identify both convex future winners and dangerous stranded-capital
situations.

Falsifiers: qualification slips, utilization remains low, customer
architectures change before the new lines fill, or fixed-cost absorption
overwhelms volume growth.

Sources:
https://www.toyogosei.co.jp/english/sustainability/message.html
https://www.toyogosei.co.jp/english/company/index.html

RANKING THIS RUN

   1. MEC / interface-chemistry density =E2=80=94 9.2/10
   2. Vacuum-content inflation =E2=80=94 8.7/10 thesis, lower current valua=
tion
   alpha in VAT itself
   3. Germanium/GeCl4 dopant scarcity =E2=80=94 8.6/10
   4. Embedded ultra-high-purity utility capacity =E2=80=94 8.3/10
   5. Prequalification-capex / Toyo Gosei =E2=80=94 8.1/10

Most important kernel additions:

   - interface_density
   - chemistry_content_per_package
   - vacuum_content_per_wafer
   - byproduct_dopant_elasticity
   - utility_lock_in
   - prequalification_capex_ratio

The strongest conceptual upgrade is CONTENT INTENSITY. We have now seen the
same pattern independently in timing, measurement, vacuum and package
chemistry: as AI hardware gets more complex, the value or quantity of
obscure enabling inputs per unit can rise faster than headline system
volumes. The kernel should therefore model d(content/unit)/dt for every
physical input, not only end-market demand growth.

Next rabbit hole: decompose MEC/VAT one layer further into qualified raw
chemicals, elastomers/seals, precision coatings and abatement components
where public-market awareness is even lower.

